Kanye West: Rapper changed his name to Ye
Rapper Kanye West changes his name on Ye.
He announced the change on Twitter on Saturday, writing: "A being formally known as Kanye West."
The forty-one-year-old West has been nicknamed Ye for some time and used the pseudonym as the title of his eighth album, which was released in June.
The change comes ahead of his appearance on Saturday Night Live, where he is expected to launch his new album Yandhi.
In the show, he replaces singer Ariana Grande, who canceled her participation for "emotional reasons," as the show's creator put it.
West has previously said that, in addition to shortening his current professional name, it also has religious significance.
“In my opinion, ‘ye’ is the most widely used word in the Bible, which means ‘you’,” West said earlier this year, referring to Big Boy.
"So it's you, it's us, it's us.
It has changed from Kanya, which means the only one, to the mere Ye – as a mere reflection of our good, our evil, our confusion, everything.
The album is a reflection of who we are.”
