The England striker tapped the ball in the penalty area back to Aguer, which beat Brighton goalkeeper Mathew Ryan with a shot into the right side of the net.
“Aguero is having problems with his feet,” City manager Pep Guardiola told reporters.
“We thought he was going to play for 55 or 60 minutes.
And that's the way it was.
We were lucky he scored a goal at that moment.”
