U.S. MEP Maxine Waters on Saturday condemned claims that a member of her staff sended the personal data of three Republican U.S. senators to the lawmakers' website.
The Los Angeles Democrat claimed the allegations were backed by "ultra-right-wing" scientists and websites.
"Lies, lies and other despicable lies," Waters said in her Twitter statement.
Published information reportedly included home addresses and phone numbers for U.S. senators. Lindsey Graham from South Carolina, and Mike Lee and Orrin Hatch, both from Utah.
