Invite your financial adviser: An adviser can help you find a way to reimburse these expenses.
Financing long-term care, for example, can be done using a traditional long-term care policy, a hybrid cash life insurance policy that will help you pay for these expenses, or with your own insurance using your own funds – as long as you have money.
Make your own legal documents: Prevent legal battles while you can.
Identify your health care representative, which will be a trusted person to supervise your medical care and ensure that doctors adhere to your wishes if you are unable to communicate.
Also, consider writing a power of attorney for your finances.
You will choose a trusted person who will make financial decisions for you and ensure the payment of your accounts in the event that you are not eligible to do so.
